  "purpose": "纯自用的球体物理回归场：地形支撑 / 台阶 / 斜面 / 台面与边缘 / 吸附物凹凸 / 挡路 / 贴墙。不是玩家关卡，不进正式场景。",
  "generated_by": "hand-authored. Geometry is NOT in this file: each wired cell points at its own placement.json, which is the single source for what exists in the scene",
  "geometry": {
    "model": "one_placement_per_cell",
    "folder": "Docs/Design/Levels/physics_test_field",
    "file": "placement.json",
    "why": "the motor's static capacity (8 planes / 8 boxes / 4 ramps) is smaller than the whole field, so the field registers one arena at a time (registration_model.mode). A cell is therefore exactly one arena, and one arena is exactly one placement document: the validator's hard budget then applies per cell, and the Unity importer binds one LevelArenaHost per document with no grouping logic to invent.",
    "fields_from_placement": [
      "structures[] (ground / boundary / box / ramp: the ONLY geometry)",
      "level.arena.id (the managed-root child and the cell's identity)",
      "level.budget (per-cell capacity, checked by levelbuild check)"
    ],
    "not_duplicated_here": "registration boxes, ramp angles, boundary planes, ground",
    "why_footprint_is_not_geometry": "cells[].footprint is the RUNNER's activation rect: it includes the run-up (C14 is 6 m wide but 12 m deep for a 6 m plate) and no placement holds it. The test suite refuses geometry that leaves its own footprint, so the rect cannot drift away from the boxes",
    "check": "python3 Tools/levelbuild/levelbuild.py check Docs/Design/Levels/physics_test_field/<cell>/placement.json",
    "preview": "source ~/tools/blender-env.sh && \"$BLENDER\" $BLENDER_FLAGS --python Tools/levelbuild/blender/render_views.py -- --placement Docs/Design/Levels/physics_test_field/<cell>/placement.json --preset plan"
  },
